WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.858 --> 00:00:18.321
struggled for breath as the fabric completely enveloped everyone.

2
00:00:18.341 --> 00:00:20.984
"Don't you ever listen, boy?"

3
00:00:21.404 --> 00:00:23.366
Wyssa's muffled voice came from nearby.

4
00:00:23.386 --> 00:00:27.249
"I'd better get us out of Galvan before you kill us all."

5
00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:29.631
Zann felt a hand grab him.

6
00:00:30.131 --> 00:00:33.169
Zap! He landed in front of the Galvan wormhole.

7
00:00:33.189 --> 00:00:38.730
"Nice work, Zann," Perda said breathlessly, as Wyssa dragged them into the wormhole.

8
00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:41.311
"You almost smothered us!"

9
00:00:43.091 --> 00:00:44.692
"Sorry," Zann mumbled.

10
00:00:45.532 --> 00:00:47.933
Once again they were speeding through the vortex.

11
00:00:47.953 --> 00:00:51.174
"How many magical worlds are there, anyway?"

12
00:00:51.474 --> 00:00:52.054
asked Perda.

13
00:00:53.014 --> 00:00:54.895
"Nobody knows," Wyssa replied.

14
00:00:54.915 --> 00:00:58.856
"The nature of wormholes makes it impossible to know for sure."

15
00:01:00.212 --> 00:01:04.573
"My parents said that hundreds of worlds have been cataloged already," Zann said.

16
00:01:04.593 --> 00:01:07.614
"But more are being discovered all the time."

17
00:01:08.514 --> 00:01:09.735
He thought about World X.

18
00:01:10.235 --> 00:01:12.916
His parents had contacted Wyssa for help in finding it.

19
00:01:13.656 --> 00:01:14.696
Did she know where it was?

20
00:01:15.516 --> 00:01:16.817
He opened his mouth to ask.

21
00:01:17.137 --> 00:01:19.177
But a flash of purple light distracted him.

22
00:01:20.018 --> 00:01:22.638
The symbols on Wyssa's hands were glowing again.

23
00:01:22.658 --> 00:01:27.560
"Oh no," Wyssa muttered when she saw the next wormhole.

24
00:01:28.416 --> 00:01:33.519
Whatever world the wormhole led to, Zann could tell she wasn't happy about going through it.

25
00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.662
He soon landed on something soft and squishy.

26
00:01:37.442 --> 00:01:42.886
Looking around, Zann could see that they were standing on a puffy white cloud floating peacefully in a

27
00:01:43.006 --> 00:01:44.447
clear golden sky.

28
00:01:45.267 --> 00:01:47.209
Dozens of similar clouds surrounded them.

29
00:01:47.229 --> 00:01:51.191
"I feel as light as a dragon's scale!"

30
00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:52.312
Perda exclaimed.

31
00:01:53.253 --> 00:01:54.433
Zann felt the same way.

32
00:01:54.994 --> 00:02:00.874
He jumped and found himself floating up surprisingly high before floating gently back down to the cloud.

33
00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:03.275
Perda did a somersault in the air.

34
00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:04.536
"Look at me!

35
00:02:05.057 --> 00:02:06.037
I'm flying!"

36
00:02:06.298 --> 00:02:06.738
she cried.

37
00:02:06.758 --> 00:02:09.100
"Settle down, both of you."

38
00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:10.641
Wyssa's voice was stern.

39
00:02:10.661 --> 00:02:13.783
"We need to figure out whether your friends are here.

40
00:02:14.263 --> 00:02:17.125
Quickly." "Okay, okay."

41
00:02:17.485 --> 00:02:19.587
Perda sat down on a fluffy patch of cloud.

42
00:02:20.387 --> 00:02:21.308
"How do we do that?"

43
00:02:21.328 --> 00:02:24.230
"I'm thinking," Wyssa said sharply.

44
00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:26.432
"Just be quiet for a moment."

45
00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:29.822
Zann bounced gently, still looking around.

46
00:02:29.842 --> 00:02:34.365
"Hey, look at that," he said, pointing at a cloud far overhead.

47
00:02:35.306 --> 00:02:39.469
It was dark and stormy, with lightning flickering through it every few seconds.

48
00:02:40.389 --> 00:02:43.731
It definitely stood out in the otherwise pale and peaceful sky.

49
00:02:43.751 --> 00:02:46.413
"I said, be quiet, boy!"

50
00:02:46.674 --> 00:02:47.314
Wyssa barked.

51
00:02:48.115 --> 00:02:49.976
Her face looked pinched and anxious.

52
00:02:50.756 --> 00:02:55.680
Before Zann could ask what was wrong, he noticed a new cloud zooming toward them.

53
00:02:56.604 --> 00:02:58.246
This one looked oddly glittery.

54
00:02:58.626 --> 00:03:00.547
When it came closer, he gasped.

55
00:03:00.567 --> 00:03:06.092
"It's a whole flock of those little stinging dragons that Morb brought to Magica!"

56
00:03:06.392 --> 00:03:06.813
he cried.

57
00:03:06.833 --> 00:03:10.235
"They're called flizzes," Wyssa said.

58
00:03:10.255 --> 00:03:14.219
"They're very useful as long as you know how to control them."

59
00:03:15.139 --> 00:03:18.782
Zann recalled the painful stings he and Darb had received from the flizzes.

60
00:03:19.603 --> 00:03:23.606
He conjured a sturdy stick to use as a weapon if the creatures came any closer.

61
00:03:23.626 --> 00:03:27.308
"You won't need that," Wyssa said with a faint smile.

62
00:03:27.328 --> 00:03:30.589
"I know exactly how to control flizzes.

63
00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:33.290
I'm the one who brought them to Morb."

64
00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:38.652
Zann wanted to ask how many other dangerous creatures Wyssa had brought to Morb.

65
00:03:39.392 --> 00:03:43.033
But before he could speak, his mouth widened into a sudden yawn.

66
00:03:44.013 --> 00:03:47.774
Lowering the stick, he sank onto the soft, welcoming cloud.

67
00:03:48.614 --> 00:03:54.276
He watched the flizzes gather around Wyssa, who began speaking softly to them in a language Zann didn't

68
00:03:54.356 --> 00:03:57.937
understand. Beside him Perda yawned as well.

69
00:03:57.957 --> 00:04:01.100
"It's been a long day, hasn't it?"

70
00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:01.880
she mumbled.

71
00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:05.202
"I think I'll just close my eyes for a second."

72
00:04:06.243 --> 00:04:09.965
Zann was drifting off to sleep too when he heard a soft snore.

73
00:04:10.886 --> 00:04:14.248
Opening his eyes, he was surprised to see Perda floating.

74
00:04:15.189 --> 00:04:17.350
Above them both was the dark cloud.

75
00:04:17.851 --> 00:04:19.552
It appeared much closer than before.

76
00:04:19.572 --> 00:04:21.673
"Weird," he mumbled.

77
00:04:22.394 --> 00:04:23.815
Wyssa heard him and looked over.

78
00:04:23.835 --> 00:04:25.576
"Oh dear," she muttered.

79
00:04:26.264 --> 00:04:28.905
"They're succumbing even faster than I'd feared."

80
00:04:30.006 --> 00:04:32.447
Glancing at the flizzes, she waved her hand.

81
00:04:32.467 --> 00:04:34.327
"Go! And hurry!"

82
00:04:35.228 --> 00:04:37.189
Zann watched the flizzes speed off.

83
00:04:38.289 --> 00:04:41.730
"Where Where are they Zann paused.

84
00:04:42.131 --> 00:04:43.871
What had he been planning to ask?

85
00:04:44.712 --> 00:04:45.432
He couldn't remember.

86
00:04:45.452 --> 00:04:47.353
"Oh well," he mumbled.

87
00:04:47.373 --> 00:04:48.673
"Doesn't matter."

88
00:04:49.634 --> 00:04:52.355
He felt himself floating upward, as Perda was doing.

89
00:04:53.175 --> 00:04:56.188
It seemed like too much trouble to resist, so he didn't.

90
00:04:56.989 --> 00:04:59.371
Besides, floating felt kind of nice.

91
00:05:00.411 --> 00:05:01.972
The stick felt heavy in his hand.

92
00:05:02.413 --> 00:05:07.096
He let it go, watching through half-closed eyes as it drifted slowly upward.

93
00:05:07.977 --> 00:05:09.578
Suddenly Zann felt a yank.

94
00:05:09.958 --> 00:05:11.759
Wyssa was pulling him back down.

95
00:05:11.779 --> 00:05:13.100
"Wake up!"

96
00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:14.501
she ordered loudly.

97
00:05:14.521 --> 00:05:15.782
"You too, girl!"

98
00:05:16.623 --> 00:05:20.645
The old woman bounced away and grabbed Perda, pulling her over to Zann's cloud.

99
00:05:21.426 --> 00:05:22.467
Perda opened her eyes.

100
00:05:22.487 --> 00:05:24.088
"What's going on?"

101
00:05:25.384 --> 00:05:27.066
Now Zann was falling back to sleep.

102
00:05:27.866 --> 00:05:31.129
Breathing desperately, Wyssa gave him a good kick to the shin.

103
00:05:31.149 --> 00:05:34.792
"Ow," Zann mumbled, scooting away from her foot.

104
00:05:35.993 --> 00:05:38.195
"I just want a quick nap, that's all."

105
00:05:38.976 --> 00:05:40.036
"You must fight it!"

106
00:05:40.297 --> 00:05:40.877
cried Wyssa.

107
00:05:41.157 --> 00:05:42.498
"Do not fall asleep!"

108
00:05:43.479 --> 00:05:45.521
Zann looked at her with half-closed eyes.

109
00:05:45.541 --> 00:05:47.102
"Did you say something?"

110
00:05:48.263 --> 00:05:51.326
He heard a snore and saw Wyssa turn her head quickly.

111
00:05:52.167 --> 00:05:53.528
Perda was floating upward again.

112
00:05:54.336 --> 00:05:56.537
The dark cloud was very close now.

113
00:05:56.557 --> 00:06:00.679
"Wake up," said Wyssa, pinching Perda.

114
00:06:01.439 --> 00:06:03.760
The old woman was beginning to sound sleepy herself.

115
00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:07.422
"Stop," Perda protested weakly.

116
00:06:08.542 --> 00:06:13.904
Zann noticed his stick was getting closer and closer to the dark cloud, which was now directly above

117
00:06:13.964 --> 00:06:19.247
him. He closed his eyes and felt his body move up off his cloud once more.

118
00:06:20.247 --> 00:06:22.088
Nearby he heard Wyssa mumbling.

119
00:06:22.868 --> 00:06:31.393
"If the flizzes don't return soon, we'll have to She slowly closed her eyes and drifted into sleep.

120
00:06:32.873 --> 00:06:33.774
Zann smiled.

121
00:06:33.794 --> 00:06:36.676
"This is so relaxing.

122
00:06:37.756 --> 00:06:42.279
I could stay here forever."

123
00:06:43.639 --> 00:06:48.642
Suddenly a bolt of magic energy shot from the dark cloud, obliterating Zann's stick.

124
00:06:49.462 --> 00:06:51.003
Zann opened his eyes for a moment.

125
00:06:51.023 --> 00:06:58.343
"What was Before he could finish, Zann fell back to sleep, unaware of the danger right above him.
